<title>TURKEY: Turkish Interbank secures $25-mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Interbank secures $25-mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's private Interbank said it had secured a $25-million syndicated loan from a group of eight banks, led by Bankers Trust and Fuji Bank.</p>
<p>The one-year pre-export financing facility carried an interest rate of 120 basis points over LIBOR, the bank said in a statement.</p>
